# Sources added by this fork on top of upstream master 4e677cb6c6ab.
#
# The entry list below is the byte-exact output of the command under "Regenerate with".
#
# Regenerate with (base = 4e677cb6c6ab, the upstream commit this fork is based on):
#   { git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- src include plugins tests/src/core tests/src/tracks \
#       | grep -E '\.(cpp|c|h|hpp|cc|cxx)$' \
#       | grep -vE '^(src/3rdparty/|plugins/NeuralAmp/rtneural/|plugins/NeuralAmp/nam/|plugins/NeuralAmp/tests/|plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/rnnoise/)' \
#       | awk '/^tests\// && !/^tests\/src\/core\/(ClipSerialisationTest|LufsMeterTest|MidiLearnTest|SessionModelTest|StemExportTest)\.(cpp|h)$/ && !/^tests\/src\/core\/StemExportTestSupport\.h$/ && !/^tests\/src\/tracks\/SampleClipWindowTest\.cpp$/ { next } { print }' ; \
#     git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- tools/local-ci.sh ; \
#   } | LC_ALL=C sort
#
# Verify it - this must print REPRODUCES and nothing else:
#   diff <(grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*(#|$)' tests/fork-sources.txt) \
#        <({ git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- src include plugins tests/src/core tests/src/tracks \
#            | grep -E '\.(cpp|c|h|hpp|cc|cxx)$' \
#            | grep -vE '^(src/3rdparty/|plugins/NeuralAmp/rtneural/|plugins/NeuralAmp/nam/|plugins/NeuralAmp/tests/|plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/rnnoise/)' \
#            | awk '/^tests\// && !/^tests\/src\/core\/(ClipSerialisationTest|LufsMeterTest|MidiLearnTest|SessionModelTest|StemExportTest)\.(cpp|h)$/ && !/^tests\/src\/core\/StemExportTestSupport\.h$/ && !/^tests\/src\/tracks\/SampleClipWindowTest\.cpp$/ { next } { print }' ; \
#          git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- tools/local-ci.sh ; \
#        } | LC_ALL=C sort) && echo REPRODUCES
#
# The pathspec is `src include plugins` (this fork's product code) plus four extras the
# product command cannot derive on its own. Each is named here with its reason, so no entry in
# this file is a hand-edit nobody can account for:
#   * tests/src/core, tests/src/tracks - the pathspec's two tests/ additions (added with them,
#     not before) - this file holds exactly seven fork-authored TEST
#     sources (LufsMeterTest, MidiLearnTest, SessionModelTest, StemExportTest,
#     StemExportTestSupport.h, ClipSerialisationTest, SampleClipWindowTest.cpp): three
#     registered by a42c68f24 (the integration fix that made Gate 9 green), two by 117068e76
#     (stem export), and two landed at integration on 2026-09-12 (ClipSerialisationTest by
#     post-alpha/clip-slice0, SampleClipWindowTest.cpp by the same lane). They are the suites of
#     fork-NEW features, so the fork ratchets look at them. The other ~100 tests/src sources
#     added since the fork point are whole-tree material and live in tests/all-sources.txt only -
#     the awk filter admits exactly these seven. A new fork test source belongs in
#     tests/all-sources.txt by default; add it to the awk pattern above only if it must carry the
#     fork ratchets too, and then re-run this command.
#
#     Merged 2026-09-12 (integration wave 3A). The two clip-lane entries arrived on the
#     integration side of this merge and were hand-added there (their lane's own comment says
#     so); the gate-hygiene side, branched before that lane landed, could not produce them. They
#     are kept rather than moved to tests/all-sources.txt for the reason this file already
#     records for tools/local-ci.sh: the fork-scoped ratchets already measure them - including
#     tests/src/tracks/SampleClipWindowTest.cpp, which holds a fork file-length baseline entry
#     (511) taken by a recorded re-anchor - and moving them would narrow the fork scope. The awk
#     allow-list above was extended by exactly those two names, and the file now reproduces from
#     the command under "Regenerate with".
#   * tools/local-ci.sh - a shell script, so outside the C/C++ extension set of the product
#     command; it is admitted by the second, explicit pathspec line above. Its extension is
#     deliberately NOT added to the first line's grep: doing so also admits five fork-authored
#     .sh harness scripts under plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/testdata/, which would widen the fork
#     scope onto shell tooling that belongs in tests/tools-sources.txt if anywhere. It is
#     registered HERE rather than in tests/tools-sources.txt because the fork-scoped ratchets
#     already measured it when that list was added, and moving it would narrow the fork scope.
#     That reason is recorded in tests/tools-sources.txt's header too.
#   * tools/stem-export-demo.py used to be a second hand-added tools/ entry in this file. It was
#     moved to tests/tools-sources.txt on 2026-09-12 (gate hygiene): tooling has one home, and
#     that list is the home tests/tools-sources.txt itself declares for tools/. It is not in the
#     command above any more, and this file no longer carries it.
#
# Why the base is a fixed commit and not `origin/master`. `origin` in this clone is
# upstream LMMS/lmms; this repo never pushes to it, and its `master` ref tracks whatever
# upstream publishes - on 2026-09-11 it was 518a7e8ef, which is NOT an ancestor of the
# fork point (verified: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/master 4e677cb6c6ab` -> 1).
# The old command as written (`... --diff-filter=A origin/master HEAD ...`) therefore
# listed 116 files instead of 109: it reclassified seven upstream files this fork
# never authored as fork-new - include/AudioOss.h, include/AudioSoundIo.h,
# include/MidiOss.h, plugins/Sf2Player/fluidsynthshims.h, src/core/audio/AudioOss.cpp,
# src/core/audio/AudioSoundIo.cpp, src/core/midi/MidiOss.cpp - all of which exist at
# 4e677cb6c6ab (`git cat-file -e 4e677cb6c6ab:<path>`). The fork point is a fixed commit,
# so the corrected command needs no remote state at all. Verify it is in the clone first:
#   git cat-file -e 4e677cb6c6ab^{commit} && echo ok
# (`git merge-base origin/master HEAD` returns the same commit - 4e677cb6c6ab - but only
# while origin has been fetched; the literal commit is the base that cannot drift.)
#
# Vendored third-party trees are excluded on purpose (524 files): src/3rdparty
# (lua, luabridge), plugins/NeuralAmp/rtneural (RTNeural), plugins/NeuralAmp/nam
# (Neural Amp Modeler), plugins/NeuralAmp/tests, plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/rnnoise
# (RNNoise). They are not this fork's code and these gates never refactor them.
#
# lcov extract patterns are anchored to the repo root (tests/run-coverage.sh
# resolves this file's directory to the repo root).
#
# The collation is pinned to C for the same reason tests/all-sources.txt's is: plain `sort`
# follows the caller's locale, so an unpinned command does not reproduce this file on a
# machine with a different one, and the tail entries appended by merge lanes ended up out of
# order for the same reason.
